font-medium transition-all text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted/50 hover:text-foreground\" href=\"/tax-data\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chart-column h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3 3v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16\"></path><path d=\"M18 17V9\"></path><path d=\"M13 17V5\"></path><path d=\"M8 17v-3\"></path></svg>Data</a><a class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-all text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted/50 hover:text-foreground\" href=\"/widgets\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-code-xml h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m18 16 4-4-4-4\"></path><path d=\"m6 8-4 4 4 4\"></path><path d=\"m14.5 4-5 16\"></path></svg>Widgets</a></nav><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><a class=\"hidden sm:flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-600 to-emerald-500 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white shadow-lg shadow-emerald-500/20 hover:shadow-emerald-500/30 transition-all hover:scale-[1.02]\" href=\"/paycheck-calculator\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chart-column h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3 3v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16\"></path><path d=\"M18 17V9\"></path><path d=\"M13 17V5\"></path><path d=\"M8 17v-3\"></path></svg>Calculate Now</a><button data-slot=\"button\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center whitespace-nowrap text-sm font-medium transition-all disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg:not([class*=&#x27;size-&#x27;])]:size-4 shrink-0 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 outline-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px] aria-invalid:ring-destructive/20 dark:aria-invalid:ring-destructive/40 aria-invalid:border-destructive hover:bg-accent dark:hover:bg-accent/50 h-8 rounded-md gap-1.5 px-3 has-[&gt;svg]:px-2.5 lg:hidden text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground\" aria-label=\"Toggle mobile menu\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-menu h-5 w-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 12h16\"></path><path d=\"M4 18h16\"></path><path d=\"M4 6h16\"></path></svg></button></div></div></header><main id=\"main-content\" class=\"flex-1\"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-8 sm:px-6 lg:px-8\"><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@graph\":[{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/relocation-calculator#webpage\",\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/relocation-calculator\",\"name\":\"Salary Relocation Calculator 2026\",\"description\":\"Free salary relocation calculator — compare take-home pay across states for your 2026 move.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\",\"dateModified\":\"2026-06-25\",\"author\":{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/relocation-calculator#author\"}},{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/relocation-calculator#breadcrumb\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Salary Relocation Calculator\"}]},{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/relocation-calculator#webapp\",\"@type\":\"WebApplication\",\"name\":\"Salary Relocation Calculator 2026\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/relocation-calculator\",\"applicationCategory\":\"FinanceApplication\",\"operatingSystem\":\"Web\",\"offers\":{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"price\":0,\"priceCurrency\":\"USD\",\"availability\":\"https://schema.org/InStock\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/relocation-calculator\"},\"author\":{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/relocation-calculator#author\"},\"publisher\":{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/#organization\"}},{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/relocation-calculator#author\",\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"Rachel Mitchell\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/about#rachel-mitchell\",\"jobTitle\":\"Lead Tax Analyst & Editorial Director, CPA\",\"description\":\"Rachel Mitchell is a Certified Public Accountant (CPA) licensed in Illinois with over 12 years of experience in individual and small-business taxation. She specializes in federal and state income tax compliance, FICA optimization, payroll tax strategy, and multi-state tax planning. Rachel holds an MS in Taxation from Golden Gate University and a BS in Accounting from the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign. She is an active member of the American Institute of Certified Public Accountants (AICPA) and the Illinois CPA Society. Before joining TheTaxCalc, Rachel spent 8 years at a Big Four accounting firm advising high-net-worth clients on tax-efficient wealth strategies.\",\"knowsAbout\":[\"Federal Income Tax\",\"State Income Tax\",\"FICA Tax\",\"Payroll Tax\",\"IRS Compliance\",\"Tax Planning\",\"Multi-State Taxation\",\"Tax-Advantaged Accounts\"],\"sameAs\":[\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/rachelmitchellcpa/\",\"https://www.aicpa-cima.com/\"],\"worksFor\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"TheTaxCalc\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com\"},\"image\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/author-rachel-mitchell.webp\"},{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/relocation-calculator#faq\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How do I calculate equivalent salary between two states?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"You've gotta look at the full picture — state income tax, property taxes, sales taxes, and overall cost of living all factor in. The basic idea is to figure out your current take-home pay after everything, then find the gross salary in the new state that gives you the same net. Our relocation calculator does this automatically so you don't have to crunch all the numbers yourself.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Is moving to a no-income-tax state always better?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Not always. States without income tax still need revenue, so they get it elsewhere — usually through higher property taxes and sales taxes. Texas is the classic example: 0% income tax but a 1.71% average property tax rate, which is nearly double Florida's 0.86%. On a $400K home, that's an extra $3,400 a year in Texas. The bottom line? Look at your total tax bill, not just income tax.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What is cost of living and why does it matter for relocation?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Cost of living is basically how much it costs to maintain your lifestyle in a given place — housing, groceries, healthcare, transportation, all of it. $100K in Texas goes way further than $100K in California because housing costs and taxes are so different. Never compare just the gross salary when you're looking at a relocation offer. The number on paper can be misleading.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How much more salary do I need to move from Texas to California?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Usually 15–25% more, depending on your income level. Someone making $100K in Texas takes home around $79K after federal tax and FICA. To get similar take-home pay in California, you'd need roughly $120K–$125K because California's income tax (1%–13.3%) can eat another $5K–$8K compared to Texas's zero. And that's before accounting for California's higher housing costs.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Does relocating affect my federal taxes?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Federal income tax and FICA stay the same no matter where you live — they're based on your income, not your zip code. What changes is your state and local tax situation, and those differences can be massive. Some states also offer different deductions and credits. So relocating doesn't touch your federal return, but it can dramatically change what ends up in your bank account.\"}}]}]}</script><nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\" class=\"mb-6 flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-muted-foreground\"><a class=\"hover:text-foreground transition-colors\" href=\"/\">Home</a><span class=\"text-muted-foreground\" aria-hidden=\"true\">/</span><span class=\"text-foreground font-medium\">Relocate</span></nav><div class=\"mb-4 flex justify-center\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"><span class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-muted-foreground\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-share2 lucide-share-2 h-3.5 w-3.5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"5\" r=\"3\"></circle><circle cx=\"6\" cy=\"12\" r=\"3\"></circle><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"19\" r=\"3\"></circle><line x1=\"8.59\" x2=\"15.42\" y1=\"13.51\" y2=\"17.49\"></line><line x1=\"15.41\" x2=\"8.59\" y1=\"6.51\" y2=\"10.49\"></line></svg>Share:</span><a href=\"https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=Relocation%20Calculator%202026%20%7C%20Compare%20Take-Home&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fthetaxcalc.com%2Frelocation-calculator&amp;via=TheTaxCalc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-border/30 p-2 transition-all hover:bg-sky-500/10 hover:text-sky-400 hover:border-sky-500/30\" aria-label=\"Share on Twitter / X\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-twitter h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M22 4s-.7 2.1-2 3.4c1.6 10-9.4 17.3-18 11.6 2.2.1 4.4-.6 6-2C3 15.5.5 9.6 3 5c2.2 2.6 5.6 4.1 9 4-.9-4.2 4-6.6 7-3.8 1.1 0 3-1.2 3-1.2z\"></path></svg></a><a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fthetaxcalc.com%2Frelocation-calculator\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-border/30 p-2 transition-all hover:bg-blue-500/10 hover:text-blue-400 hover:border-blue-500/30\" aria-label=\"Share on LinkedIn\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-linkedin h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M16 8a6 6 0 0 1 6 6v7h-4v-7a2 2 0 0 0-2-2 2 2 0 0 0-2 2v7h-4v-7a6 6 0 0 1 6-6z\"></path><rect width=\"4\" height=\"12\" x=\"2\" y=\"9\"></rect><circle cx=\"4\" cy=\"4\" r=\"2\"></circle></svg></a><button data-slot=\"button\" class=\"justify-center whitespace-nowrap font-medium disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg:not([class*=&#x27;size-&#x27;])]:size-4 shrink-0 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 outline-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px] aria-invalid:ring-destructive/20 dark:aria-invalid:ring-destructive/40 aria-invalid:border-destructive hover:text-accent-foreground dark:hover:bg-accent/50 h-8 has-[&gt;svg]:px-2.5 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-border/30 px-3 py-2 text-xs transition-all hover:bg-muted/50\" aria-label=\"Copy link\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-link2 lucide-link-2 h-3.5 w-3.5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M9 17H7A5 5 0 0 1 7 7h2\"></path><path d=\"M15 7h2a5 5 0 1 1 0 10h-2\"></path><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"16\" y1=\"12\" y2=\"12\"></line></svg>Copy Link</button></div></div><div class=\"mb-8 text-center\"><h1 class=\"text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-4xl\">Free Relocation Calculator</h1><p class=\"mt-2 text-muted-foreground max-w-2xl mx-auto\">Free relocation salary calculator for 2026. Compare take-home pay in IL, TX, FL, CA, NY. Find the salary you need to maintain your lifestyle. No sign-up.</p><p class=\"mt-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground\">Last reviewed: January 2026 · Tax data verified against IRS Publication 15-T &amp; state revenue departments</p></div><!--$!--><template data-dgst=\"BAILOUT_TO_CLIENT_SIDE_RENDERING\"></template><div class=\"space-y-6\"><div class=\"grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-5\"><div class=\"space-y-4 lg:col-span-3\"><div class=\"rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-6\"><div data-slot=\"skeleton\" class=\"bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-6 w-40 mb-4\"></div><div class=\"space-y-4\"><div data-slot=\"skeleton\" class=\"bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-10 w-full\"></div><div data-slot=\"skeleton\" class=\"bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-10 w-full\"></div><div data-slot=\"skeleton\" class=\"bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-10 w-2/3\"></div></div></div></div><div class=\"lg:col-span-2\"><div class=\"rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-6\"><div data-slot=\"skeleton\" class=\"bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-6 w-32 mb-4\"></div><div data-slot=\"skeleton\" class=\"bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-20 w-full mb-4\"></div><div data-slot=\"skeleton\" class=\"bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-4 w-full\"></div><div data-slot=\"skeleton\" class=\"bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-4 w-3/4\"></div><div data-slot=\"skeleton\" class=\"bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md h-4 w-1/2\"></div></div></div></div></div><!--/$--><section class=\"mt-8 rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-emerald-500/5 p-6 sm:p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-foreground mb-3\">Related Tools &amp; Resources</h2><div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2\"><a class=\"flex items-start gap-2 rounded-lg p-2 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 transition-colors\" href=\"/paycheck-calculator\"><span>💵</span><div><span class=\"text-sm font-medium text-foreground\">Paycheck Calculator</span><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground\">Full breakdown for any state</p></div></a><a class=\"flex items-start gap-2 rounded-lg p-2 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 transition-colors\" href=\"/compare\"><span>📊</span><div><span class=\"text-sm font-medium text-foreground\">State Comparison</span><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground\">Side-by-side tax comparison</p></div></a><a class=\"flex items-start gap-2 rounded-lg p-2 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 transition-colors\" href=\"/mortgage-calculator\"><span>🏠</span><div><span class=\"text-sm font-medium text-foreground\">Mortgage Calculator</span><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground\">Housing costs in your new state</p></div></a><a class=\"flex items-start gap-2 rounded-lg p-2 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 transition-colors\" href=\"/salary\"><span>💰</span><div><span class=\"text-sm font-medium text-foreground\">Salary After Tax</span><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground\">Take-home for every salary level</p></div></a></div></section><div class=\"mt-12 space-y-10\"><section class=\"rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-6 sm:p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\">How This Calculator Works</h2><div class=\"space-y-4\"><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">My sister got a job offer in San Francisco that paid $15,000 more than her Chicago salary. Sounded great until she ran the numbers. After California state tax and higher housing costs, she'd actually have less money left over. That's exactly what this calculator prevents. It tells you the salary you'd need in a new state to match your current take-home pay.</p><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">How it works: first we calculate your current take-home after federal tax, FICA, and your state's income tax. Then we figure out what gross salary in the target state would give you the same net pay, accounting for that state's tax rates and deductions.</p><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Let's look at a real example. $100,000 in Texas (0% state tax) gets you roughly $79,000 take-home. To end up with the same $79,000 in California, you'd need to earn about $120,000–$125,000. California's progressive income tax eats an extra $5,000–$8,000 that Texas doesn't touch. That's a car payment, a vacation, or a decent chunk of retirement savings — just gone to state tax.</p><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">This tool focuses on income tax differences. But look, income tax isn't the whole story:<br/>- Property taxes: <a href=\"/texas-tax-calculator\">Texas</a> is brutal (~1.71%), <a href=\"/california-tax-calculator\">California</a> is surprisingly mild (~0.71%)<br/>- Sales taxes vary significantly by state and city<br/>- Housing costs are the big one — $1,500/month in Houston can be $3,000 in San Francisco<br/>Check our <a href=\"/compare\">state comparison pages</a> for the full picture.</p></div></section><section class=\"rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-emerald-500/5 p-6 sm:p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\">How It&#x27;s Calculated</h2><div class=\"space-y-5\"><div><h3 class=\"text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 mb-2\">Formula</h3><div class=\"rounded-lg bg-background/50 border border-border/30 p-4 font-mono text-sm text-foreground\">Equivalent Salary = Current Net Pay ÷ (1 − New State Effective Tax Rate)</div></div><div><h3 class=\"text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 mb-2\">Step-by-Step</h3><ol class=\"space-y-2\"><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\"><span class=\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/20 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\">1</span><span class=\"leading-relaxed\">Calculate your current take-home pay in your current state</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\"><span class=\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/20 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\">2</span><span class=\"leading-relaxed\">Determine the effective tax rate in the new state (federal + state + local)</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\"><span class=\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/20 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\">3</span><span class=\"leading-relaxed\">Calculate the salary needed in the new state to match current net pay</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\"><span class=\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/20 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\">4</span><span class=\"leading-relaxed\">Factor in cost-of-living differences (housing, sales tax, property tax)</span></li><li class=\"flex gap-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\"><span class=\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/20 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\">5</span><span class=\"leading-relaxed\">Compare side-by-side: current state vs. new state net pay at same salary</span></li></ol></div><div><h3 class=\"text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 mb-2\">Example</h3><div class=\"rounded-lg bg-background/50 border border-border/30 p-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Taking home $61,600 in Texas on $75K salary. Moving to Illinois: Need ≈ $82,000 salary to maintain same net pay due to 4.95% state tax.</div></div><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground\">For detailed data sources and full methodology, see our <a class=\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\" href=\"/methodology\">Methodology &amp; Data Sources</a> page.</p></div></section><section class=\"rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-emerald-500/5 p-6 sm:p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\">Key Rates &amp; Data for 2026</h2><div class=\"grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3\"><div class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/60 p-4\"><p class=\"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground mb-1\">States Covered</p><p class=\"text-base font-bold text-foreground\">IL, TX, FL, CA, NY</p></div><div class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/60 p-4\"><p class=\"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground mb-1\">IL Flat Rate</p><p class=\"text-base font-bold text-foreground\">4.95%</p></div><div class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/60 p-4\"><p class=\"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground mb-1\">TX / FL Rate</p><p class=\"text-base font-bold text-foreground\">0%</p></div><div class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/60 p-4\"><p class=\"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground mb-1\">CA Top Rate</p><p class=\"text-base font-bold text-foreground\">13.3%</p></div><div class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/60 p-4\"><p class=\"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground mb-1\">NY Top Rate (+ NYC)</p><p class=\"text-base font-bold text-foreground\">10.9% + 3.876%</p></div></div></section><section><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6\">Relocation Calculator FAQ</h2><div class=\"space-y-3\"><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\"><h3 class=\"text-sm sm:text-base\">How do I calculate equivalent salary between two states?</h3><svg class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M19 9l-7 7-7-7\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">You&#x27;ve gotta look at the full picture — state income tax, property taxes, sales taxes, and overall cost of living all factor in. The basic idea is to figure out your current take-home pay after everything, then find the gross salary in the new state that gives you the same net. Our relocation calculator does this automatically so you don&#x27;t have to crunch all the numbers yourself.</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\"><h3 class=\"text-sm sm:text-base\">Is moving to a no-income-tax state always better?</h3><svg class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M19 9l-7 7-7-7\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Not always. States without income tax still need revenue, so they get it elsewhere — usually through higher property taxes and sales taxes. Texas is the classic example: 0% income tax but a 1.71% average property tax rate, which is nearly double Florida&#x27;s 0.86%. On a $400K home, that&#x27;s an extra $3,400 a year in Texas. The bottom line? Look at your total tax bill, not just income tax.</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\"><h3 class=\"text-sm sm:text-base\">What is cost of living and why does it matter for relocation?</h3><svg class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M19 9l-7 7-7-7\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Cost of living is basically how much it costs to maintain your lifestyle in a given place — housing, groceries, healthcare, transportation, all of it. $100K in Texas goes way further than $100K in California because housing costs and taxes are so different. Never compare just the gross salary when you&#x27;re looking at a relocation offer. The number on paper can be misleading.</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\"><h3 class=\"text-sm sm:text-base\">How much more salary do I need to move from Texas to California?</h3><svg class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M19 9l-7 7-7-7\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Usually 15–25% more, depending on your income level. Someone making $100K in Texas takes home around $79K after federal tax and FICA. To get similar take-home pay in California, you&#x27;d need roughly $120K–$125K because California&#x27;s income tax (1%–13.3%) can eat another $5K–$8K compared to Texas&#x27;s zero. And that&#x27;s before accounting for California&#x27;s higher housing costs.</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 overflow-hidden\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 text-left font-medium text-foreground hover:bg-muted/10 transition-colors\"><h3 class=\"text-sm sm:text-base\">Does relocating affect my federal taxes?</h3><svg class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform group-open:rotate-180\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M19 9l-7 7-7-7\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Federal income tax and FICA stay the same no matter where you live — they&#x27;re based on your income, not your zip code. What changes is your state and local tax situation, and those differences can be massive. Some states also offer different deductions and credits. So relocating doesn&#x27;t touch your federal return, but it can dramatically change what ends up in your bank account.</div></details></div></section><section class=\"rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-6 sm:p-8\"><p class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-foreground mb-4\">Related Articles</p><div class=\"grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3\"><a class=\"group rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/60 p-4 hover:border-emerald-500/30 hover:bg-emerald-500/5 transition-all\" href=\"/blog/florida-vs-texas-tax-comparison\"><h3 class=\"text-sm font-semibold text-foreground group-hover:text-emerald-400 transition-colors mb-1\">Florida vs Texas Tax Comparison</h3><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed line-clamp-2\">A detailed comparison of the tax structures in Florida and Texas — two of the most popular no-income-tax states for relocation.</p></a><a class=\"group rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/60 p-4 hover:border-emerald-500/30 hover:bg-emerald-500/5 transition-all\" href=\"/blog/why-texas-has-no-income-tax\"><h3 class=\"text-sm font-semibold text-foreground group-hover:text-emerald-400 transition-colors mb-1\">Why Texas Has No Income Tax</h3><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed line-clamp-2\">How Texas funds its government without a personal income tax, and what it means for residents in terms of property taxes and overall tax burden.</p></a></div></section><section class=\"rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-6 sm:p-8\"><p class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-foreground mb-4\">Related Calculators</p><div class=\"flex flex-wrap gap-3\"><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-500/5 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-emerald-400 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 hover:border-emerald-500/50 transition-all\" href=\"/paycheck-calculator\"><svg class=\"h-3.5 w-3.5\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M13 7l5 5m0 0l-5 5m5-5H6\"></path></svg>Paycheck Calculator</a><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-500/5 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-emerald-400 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 hover:border-emerald-500/50 transition-all\" href=\"/illinois-tax-calculator\"><svg class=\"h-3.5 w-3.5\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M13 7l5 5m0 0l-5 5m5-5H6\"></path></svg>Illinois Calculator</a><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-500/5 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-emerald-400 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 hover:border-emerald-500/50 transition-all\" href=\"/texas-tax-calculator\"><svg class=\"h-3.5 w-3.5\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\" st